<title>UK: BP Q4 replacement cost profit 689 mln stg.</title>
<headline>BP Q4 replacement cost profit 689 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>				 (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence, replacement) 12.2		 vs 9.0</p>
<p> Shr (pence, historic)    8.5		  vs 3.0 loss</p>
<p> Final dividend (pence)   5.25		 vs 4.25</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)   19.50		vs 15.25</p>
<p>Replacement cost net</p>
<p>    before exceptionals   689		  vs 501</p>
<p>Historic cost net</p>
<p>    after exceptionals    479		  vs 160 loss</p>
<p>			     - Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p> Shr (pence, replacement) 46.7		 vs 36.3</p>
<p>Replacement cost net</p>
<p>    before exceptionals   2,620		vs 2,103</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the British oil group is British Petroleum Plc. Analysts had forecast replacement cost net profits before exceptional items for 1996 between 2.5 billion and 2.75 billion stg.  </p>
<p>				   - Three months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p> Exceptional charge	 367		  vs 667</p>
<p> Interest paid		86		   vs 105</p>
<p> Pretax profit		737		  vs 36 loss</p>
<p> Tax			    258		  vs 140</p>
<p> Stockholding gains	 157		  vs 6</p>
<p>Operating profits by sector</p>
<p> - Exploration/production 814		  vs 579</p>
<p> - Refining/marketing     163		  vs 69</p>
<p> - Chemicals		  104		  vs 127</p>
<p> - Other business	   7 loss	     vs 5</p>
<p>NOTE - The exceptional charge is after taxation.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
